# carbon_fscatinfo_shim.c / carbon_fscatinfo_tramp.asm — the classic File
# Manager's FSCatalogInfo family. These symbols EXIST natively; what abigen gets
# wrong is the SHAPE. FSCatalogInfo is 144 bytes on i386 and 148 on x86_64
# (FSPermissionInfo ends in an FSFileSecurityRef POINTER), so typeconv routes it
# to the deep-copy path, which stages the pointee in a scratch slot of the shim
# frame sized for exactly ONE struct. Right for the single-item calls; fatal for
# the BULK ones, where the native callee fills `actualObjects` entries and
# overruns the frame straight into the i386 caller's locals (measured on Civ IV:
# 11 * 148 bytes into an 880-byte frame; the caller's two `operator new[]`
# pointers read back NULL and it SIGSEGVs dereferencing one). abigen's field walk
# also strides UTCDateTime by 12 (the natural size) instead of the packed 8, so
# every date/size/valence field lands at the wrong offset even for one struct.
_FSGetCatalogInfoBulk
_FSCatalogSearch
_FSGetCatalogInfo
_FSSetCatalogInfo
_FSCreateFileUnicode
_FSCreateDirectoryUnicode
_FSCreateFileAndOpenForkUnicode

